    "created_at": "2018-06-26T23:03:35Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-06-26T23:03:35Z",
    "body": "Hmm. This isn't horrible: basically, if we don't have a definition, we want to preserve the `is`, so that later if we get upgraded, it's still there. Whereas if we have a definition, we know this is useless, so we throw it away...\r\n\r\nI can see how it's a bit weird though. What would your preferred solution be?",
